The Internet Archive allows the public to upload and download digital material to its data cluster, but the bulk of its data is collected automatically by its web crawlers, which work to preserve as much of the public web as possible. The Wayback Machine, its web archive, contains more than 1 trillion web captures.[8][9] The Archive also oversees numerous book digitization projects, collectively one of the world's largest book digitization efforts. The Archive is used frequently by journalists and Wikipedia editors.[10][11][12]

